# ---- Runtime storage and client data — never commit ----
# Everything under backend/data/ is runtime state or real client material:
# uploaded ROAR decks, extracted ROI records, and the SME audit log. Postgres and
# the object store are the actual stores; the JSON files here are only a local
# dev fallback and a one-time migration source.
#
# This was previously a list of individual paths, which missed two things: the
# audit log is audit_log.json (the rule said audit_events.json), and the files
# had already been committed — gitignore does not apply to tracked files, so
# they kept updating. They were untracked with `git rm -r --cached backend/data/`;
# the directory rule below is what stops it happening again.
backend/data/
